      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe chat benchmark lets `extra_request_body` override `stream`, but response decoding still follows the CLI default. Setting `stream=false` can report a successful request with empty generated text; the reverse override attempts to decode SSE as JSON and fails.\n\n## Modifications\n\nUse the final payload's `stream` value to select JSON/SSE decoding, and the same override precedence when multi-turn requests default `stream_options.include_usage`. Extend the existing HTTP-backed prompt-length suite to cover both directions, preserve generated text and per-round usage, and check that the caller's body is unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model-forward or inference-engine behavior is changed. CPU tests use a local HTTP server that chooses JSON or SSE from the actual received request.\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  test/registered/unit/bench/test_bench_serving_prompt_len.py \\\n  test/registered/bench_fn/test_bench_serving_reasoning_stream.py -q\n\nPATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\n  python/sglang/benchmark/serving.py \\\n  test/registered/unit/bench/test_bench_serving_prompt_len.py\n\ngit diff --check origin/main..HEAD\n```\n\nmacOS arm64 / Python 3.12.13: **14 tests and 12 subtests pass**, with normal package imports and no validation launcher. All applicable configured hooks pass. The four added override subcases fail against unchanged upstream source: two lose generated text, and two raise `ContentTypeError`. No model weights or accelerator execution are involved.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThis corrects benchmark-client response handling. No inference speed benchmark or performance gain is claimed.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Run configured pre-commit hooks on the changed files.\n- [x] Add regression coverage to an existing registered CPU suite.\n- [x] Follow SGLang code style.\n- Documentation: existing request override behavior is preserved; no new option.\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate, implement and validate this patch. Open PR titles and nearby benchmark patches were checked, including #24272, #43209, #43217, #43219, #39866, #41403, #43894 and #36272. They address other behaviors and retain the affected JSON/SSE mode selection.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38526215126](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38526215126)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38526215099](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38526215099)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38526215136](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38526215136)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
